k-expert-skip-quality_help
usage: k-expert-skip-quality [-h] --model MODEL
                             (--articles ARTICLES | --tokenized-windows TOKENIZED_WINDOWS)
                             --output OUTPUT [--batch BATCH] [--tokens TOKENS]
                             [--prefix-tokens PREFIX_TOKENS]
                             [--limit-docs LIMIT_DOCS]
                             [--limit-windows LIMIT_WINDOWS]
                             [--arms ARMS [ARMS ...] | --arms-file ARMS_FILE]
                             [--gate-threshold GATE_THRESHOLD]
                             [--tail-rank TAIL_RANK]
                             [--policy-backend {torch,triton,triton_multi}]
                             [--dtype DTYPE] [--quantization QUANTIZATION]
                             [--gpu-memory-utilization GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION]
                             [--reference-max-mib REFERENCE_MAX_MIB]
                             [--seed SEED] [--trust-remote-code]
                             [--identity-tolerance IDENTITY_TOLERANCE]

Controlled vLLM decode teacher-forced quality, not a speed benchmark. Example
(GPU execution belongs to the main session's lock wrapper): python
quality_decode.py --model /path/to/OLMoE --articles validation.jsonl --output
quality_b8.json --batch 8 --tokens 32 --prefix-tokens 128 --limit-docs 16
--arms dense global1 global2 global4 gate05 marginal05 --tokens counts genuine
decode predictions. One extra forced token is emitted from the prefill
prediction and retained separately, excluded from summaries. PPL describes the
selected fixed-length WikiText decode windows; it is not the standard whole-
corpus WikiText PPL or a free-generation task-quality result. Alternatively
--tokenized-windows takes prepare_wikitext_rolling.py's manifest and evaluates
all windows by default, including the short tail/incomplete batch. Its prefix
includes one excluded prefill bridge: a context of P tokens uses an engine
prompt of P-1, then scores every source position [P,N) in true decode. This is
rolling PPL under the manifest's declared context resets, not independent
article samples or an equivalence claim to other standard context protocols.
The loaded router's normalization is preserved. In the inspected OLMoE vLLM
path renormalize=False: dropped weights become zero and surviving weights are
unchanged; normalized gate fractions are used only for eligibility/budgeting.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODEL
  --articles ARTICLES   Original article-text JSONL workflow
  --tokenized-windows TOKENIZED_WINDOWS
                        Rolling manifest.json; exact token IDs, tokenizer
                        identity checked; all windows by default
  --output OUTPUT
  --batch BATCH
  --tokens TOKENS       Text input only: scored decode tokens per article
  --prefix-tokens PREFIX_TOKENS
                        Text input only: engine prompt length
  --limit-docs LIMIT_DOCS
                        Text input only: article selection limit
  --limit-windows LIMIT_WINDOWS
                        Rolling input only: explicit exploratory prefix;
                        default evaluates complete split coverage
  --arms ARMS [ARMS ...]
  --arms-file ARMS_FILE
                        JSON arms list with arbitrary explicit SkipConfig
                        specs; native added automatically
  --gate-threshold GATE_THRESHOLD
  --tail-rank TAIL_RANK
                        Zero-based actual-weight rank threshold
  --policy-backend {torch,triton,triton_multi}
  --dtype DTYPE
  --quantization QUANTIZATION
  --gpu-memory-utilization GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION
  --reference-max-mib REFERENCE_MAX_MIB
  --seed SEED
  --trust-remote-code
  --identity-tolerance IDENTITY_TOLERANCE

