k-expert-skip-generate_help
usage: k-expert-skip-generate [-h] --model MODEL --output OUTPUT
                              [--arms-file ARMS_FILE] [--batch BATCH]
                              [--max-tokens MAX_TOKENS]
                              [--max-model-len MAX_MODEL_LEN] [--dtype DTYPE]
                              [--quantization QUANTIZATION]
                              [--gpu-memory-utilization GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION]
                              [--seed SEED] [--trust-remote-code] --prompts
                              PROMPTS [--limit LIMIT]
                              [--prompt-tokens PROMPT_TOKENS]
                              [--temperature TEMPERATURE] [--top-p TOP_P]

Natural-termination paired generation, not a throughput benchmark. Default
target: 200 distinct prompts for every arm. EOS is enabled; no forced tokens,
minimum output length, or repetition penalty. Cohorts drain naturally, so
--batch is an admission ceiling, not a constant decode batch size. Use the
main session's external GPU lock. --self-test is dependency-free and CPU-only.
vLLM 0.26 interfaces: https://github.com/vllm-
project/vllm/blob/v0.26.0/vllm/v1/engine/llm_engine.py and
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.26.0/vllm/outputs.py

