k-expert-skip-eval_help
usage: k-expert-skip-eval [-h] {prepare,standard,adapted} ...

Task quality entry points for lm-eval 0.4.13 and vLLM 0.26.0. prepare: CPU-
only, pin the four official task dataset repos to immutable HF commits, cache
them under --data-dir, export explicit generation adaptations. standard:
official MMLU 5-shot, GSM8K 5-shot, HellaSwag 0-shot and ARC-c 0-shot.
MMLU/HellaSwag/ARC-c use prompt loglikelihood and are identity controls for a
decode-only intervention, NOT evidence that generated task quality is safe.
GSM8K's official generate_until evaluation does exercise decode. adapted:
separately labelled MC generation adaptation (brief reasoning then "Final
answer: A"). First-token-only answers still do not exercise decode. All
inference uses an existing local model, offline datasets, identical samples
and prompt hashes across arms, and the main session's external GPU lock. No
forced length or ignore_eos. --limit is per leaf task (including each MMLU
subject); the default is the full task. --self-test uses CPU stdlib only.
Official APIs checked against installed lm_eval 0.4.13 and these sources:
https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-
harness/blob/main/lm_eval/evaluator.py https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-
evaluation-harness/blob/main/lm_eval/models/vllm_causallms.py
https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-
harness/tree/main/lm_eval/tasks/mmlu https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-
evaluation-harness/tree/main/lm_eval/tasks/gsm8k
https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-
harness/tree/main/lm_eval/tasks/hellaswag https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-
evaluation-harness/tree/main/lm_eval/tasks/arc

positional arguments:
  {prepare,standard,adapted}
    prepare             CPU-only task dataset preparation, no model loading

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit

k-expert-skip-prepare-rolling_help
usage: k-expert-skip-prepare-rolling [-h] --model MODEL
                                     [--source-manifest SOURCE_MANIFEST]
                                     [--parquet PARQUET]
                                     [--split {validation,test}]
                                     [--prefix-tokens PREFIX_TOKENS]
                                     [--scored-tokens SCORED_TOKENS]
                                     --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
                                     [--trust-remote-code]

Build a complete local WikiText split into pretokenized decode-quality
windows. Rows are joined in original parquet order with exactly two newlines,
including empty rows; the resulting text is tokenized once, without special
tokens. For prefix P and score length S, score [P,N) exactly once in adjacent
spans of at most S tokens. Each window resets its history to the preceding P
tokens. The engine receives P-1 prompt tokens and emits the final context
token from prefill (excluded); all S scored predictions therefore occur in
real decode. These windows are not independent articles, and this declared
rolling-context PPL is not asserted equivalent to other WikiText evaluation
protocols.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODEL         Local model/tokenizer directory; no weights are loaded
  --source-manifest SOURCE_MANIFEST
                        Original split provenance manifest; required outside a
                        checkout with bundled local dataset provenance
  --parquet PARQUET     Local original parquet; must match the split SHA in
                        source-manifest
  --split {validation,test}
  --prefix-tokens PREFIX_TOKENS
                        Context at first scored token, including one excluded
                        prefill bridge; engine prompt is P-1
  --scored-tokens SCORED_TOKENS
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --trust-remote-code

k-expert-skip-tune_help
usage: k-expert-skip-tune [-h] --model MODEL --traces TRACES [TRACES ...]
                          --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
                          [--batches BATCHES [BATCHES ...]] [--layer LAYER]
                          [--quantization {bf16,fp8}]
                          [--events-per-batch EVENTS_PER_BATCH]
                          [--rounds ROUNDS]
                          [--replays-per-sample REPLAYS_PER_SAMPLE]
                          [--evict-mib EVICT_MIB] [--seed SEED]
                          [--max-relative-l2 MAX_RELATIVE_L2] [--plan-only]

Small, native-only BF16/online-FP8 Triton MoE tuning grid for vLLM 0.26. Run
GPU work only through run_locked.py. --plan-only is CPU-only and checks actual
native route coverage without importing torch/vLLM. Real local OLMoE,
Qwen3-MoE or DeepSeek-V2-Lite routed-expert weights are assembled read-only.
The default is the first MoE layer (0 for OLMoE/Qwen3, 1 for
DeepSeek-V2-Lite); DeepSeek's dense and shared experts are excluded.
Activations are synthetic standard-normal BF16 and are explicitly not captured
model activations. --quantization fp8 invokes vLLM's actual online per-tensor
weight conversion on this BF16 layer, then its TRITON layout and quant-config
builders. Dynamic FP8 activation quantization is part of the measured expert
block. Supply native traces from the intended model/format: route
shapes/provenance are checked, but this script cannot infer the numerical
format of every input trace artifact. The objective is native top-k expert-
block latency, not post-skip latency. All comparison arms must use the SAME
emitted VLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER in a fresh engine. CUDA graph timing includes
alignment, both GEMMs, activation, and reduction. It excludes router
selection, CPU dispatch, and policy work. Repeated cache conditioning is a
declared approximation, not proof of cold DRAM. A selected tile is a kernel
tuning result, not a service speedup claim.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --model MODEL
  --traces TRACES [TRACES ...]
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --batches BATCHES [BATCHES ...]
  --layer LAYER         Default: first routed MoE layer from config
                        (DeepSeek-V2-Lite: 1; OLMoE/Qwen3: 0)
  --quantization {bf16,fp8}
                        BF16 by default; fp8 uses native vLLM online per-
                        tensor W8A8 conversion of the same checkpoint
  --events-per-batch EVENTS_PER_BATCH
  --rounds ROUNDS
  --replays-per-sample REPLAYS_PER_SAMPLE
  --evict-mib EVICT_MIB
  --seed SEED
  --max-relative-l2 MAX_RELATIVE_L2
  --plan-only

